<section class="lf-guide-faq">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details><summary>Are Facebook ads effective for Christmas light installers?</summary><p>They can be effective when the offer, visuals, local market and lead-handling process are aligned. Performance depends on competition, budget, audience and execution.</p></details>
<details><summary>Should I run image ads or video ads?</summary><p>Test both. Images can show the finished result quickly, while video and Reels can demonstrate transformations and the installation experience.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Facebook ads generate qualified Christmas lighting leads?</summary><p>Yes, but qualification requires checking service area, project scope, budget and timing rather than counting all submitted forms equally.</p></details>
<details><summary>Should I use Meta instant forms or a website landing page?</summary><p>Both can work. Choose based on the amount of explanation and qualification needed, and compare downstream lead quality.</p></details>
<details><summary>What happens after someone requests a Christmas lighting quote?</summary><p>A connected system should capture the inquiry, record its source, assign an owner and provide a suitable booking or quote next step.</p></details>
    </section>

